## Fallback — only if Sentinel can't satisfy the requirement
If Sentinel can't be made to work/evidence this, **or** a customer/auditor insists on an actual **IDPS** (not just a firewall), upgrade the firewall:
- `terraform/modules/azure/firewall.tf`: `sku_tier = "Premium"` and add an `intrusion_detection` block (`mode = "Alert"` or `"Deny"`).
- Traffic is already routed through the firewall, so no routing changes needed.
- ~€1,200–1,500/mo. This gives a literal signature-based IDS/IPS.

**Note:** Standard firewall + threat-intel Deny ≠ IDPS. IDPS is Premium-only. If the need is a real IDPS, Sentinel (detection-only) does **not** cover inline *prevention* — only Premium IDPS in Deny mode does.
